/* DATA DESCRIPTION:
Citation:	Cobb, Alexander R; Harvey, Charles Franklin (2019): Water level data of mdm trail 8 from the Mendaram peat swamp in Brunei Darussalam [dataset]. PANGAEA, https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.908207, 
	In supplement to: Cobb, AR; Harvey, CF (2019): Scalar Simulation and Parameterization of Water Table Dynamics in Tropical Peatlands. Water Resources Research, 55(11), 9351-9377, https://doi.org/10.1029/2019WR025411
Abstract:	Water level data were obtained from logging pressure transducers (Solinst Levelogger Edge 3001, Solinst Canada, Georgetown, Ontario, Canada) corrected for barometeric fluctuations using a barometer (Solinst Barologger Gold 3001). Each transducer was suspended on a steel cable inside a 2" PVC pipe 1.5 m in length installed to 1.4 m depth and screened at 1.3--1.45 m below the top of the piezometer casing. Piezometers were developed prior to measurement by repeatedly plunging and removing a solid rod into the piezometer tube. The details of how the surface datum was obtained are described in Cobb et al (2017, doi:10.1073/pnas.1701090114).
Keyword(s):	hydraulic conductivity; specific yield; throughfall; tropical peat swamp; water table
Further details:	README for Brunei peat swamp data (URI: https://store.pangaea.de/Publications/Cobb-Harvey_2019/README.pdf)
Coverage:	LATITUDE: 4.371105 * LONGITUDE: 114.354700
	DATE/TIME START: 2012-02-06T22:20:00 * DATE/TIME END: 2013-01-30T02:40:00
Event(s):	Brunei_Darussalam_mdm_trail_8 * LATITUDE: 4.371105 * LONGITUDE: 114.354700
Parameter(s):	DATE/TIME (Date/Time) * GEOCODE * PI: Cobb, Alexander R (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3128-3002, alex.cobb@smart.mit.edu) * METHOD/DEVICE: Solinst Levelogger (URI: http://www.solinst.com/Prod/3001/3001.html)
	Water level [m] (WL) * PI: Cobb, Alexander R (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3128-3002, alex.cobb@smart.mit.edu) * METHOD/DEVICE: Solinst Levelogger (URI: http://www.solinst.com/Prod/3001/3001.html)
